```
*Voicing the option you rejected — and why — is what signals real judgement.*

```java
// Original: SpotSize-based spots. New ask: EV charging.
// Extend via a capability interface -- existing ParkingSpot untouched.
interface Chargeable { void startCharging(Vehicle v); }

class ElectricChargingSpot extends ParkingSpot implements Chargeable {
    public void startCharging(Vehicle v) { /* meter + bill kWh */ }
}
// ParkingLot only needs to know about Chargeable where charging matters.
```
*A new subclass + capability interface absorbs the requirement without editing existing spots (OCP).*

```java
// ISP: small capability interfaces instead of one fat IVehicle
interface Parkable { boolean park(ParkingSpot s); }
interface Chargeable { void charge(); }

// LSP: every subtype honours the Vehicle contract -- no surprise throws
abstract class Vehicle { abstract SpotSize requiredSize(); }
class Motorcycle extends Vehicle { SpotSize requiredSize() { return SpotSize.COMPACT; } }

// DIP: depend on the abstraction, inject it
class ParkingLot { ParkingLot(FeeCalculator fee) { /* ... */ } }
```
*Each line is a normal design decision that happens to embody a SOLID principle.*
